      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It still seems to work fine on my end. Eye tracking is fully set up, but the \"blink\" shape keys are blank. I have an Animator component on Body that controls a separate \"Blink\" blend shape.\n\nI have to perform some weird animator behavior keyframe magic to toggle the blink on/off though, but that has always been the case. (Trying to alter the blink shape key directly in a gesture override breaks blinking even if the gesture is currently not used)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-05-19T01:59:32.424Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Prior to build 772, you were able to do things such as put an animator on your mesh to control blinking, as well as let the eye tracking control your eye movements. \n\nPeople would do this so that you could have gestures to close your eyes, without doubling up on the blinks, causing the model's face to look bad every time it blinks. \n\nThis was fixed by renaming my Mesh to \"Body_\" which obviously stops the eye tracking entirely. \n\nFor the setup: \n\nMy mesh has two sets of blink blendshapes, one made for eye tracking when I was using it, and the raw blendshapes that I made prior. \n\nI control the raw blendshapes with the animator, and do not touch vrc.blink_L or R. \n\nThis was tested with and without eye bones being assigned in Mecanim. Both result in the animator not working. It may be getting stripped off of any mesh named \"Body\" but I am unsure.",
